WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.467
-Now, usually when we start
"A Closer Look,"

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.667
we tell you at the top

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.100
which news stories
we're about to cover.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.968
Obviously, we have a bit more
than usual to catch up on today,

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:12.734
so just bear with me
while I try to get through this.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.534
Donald Trump appeared
in a Manhattan courthouse today

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.667
for a fraud trial after a judge
ruled that he and his family

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.334
had lied about their
business assets for years.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:19.767
House Republicans
descend into chaos

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.667
and finger-pointing after nearly
shutting down the government

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.167
while simultaneously
embarrassing themselves

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.434
with the sham
impeachment inquiry

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:26.000
into Joe Biden
that even their own witnesses

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.367
admitted did not have
any evidence.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:28.534
Florida Congressman
Matt Gaetz announced

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:29.567
that he'll try to remove

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:30.667
Kevin McCarthy
as Speaker of the House.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:31.968
Trump is preparing
for another hearing

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.701
over a proposed gag order
to stop him

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:36.100
from making threats in the run
up to a criminal trial.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.000
Attempted coup trial dates
have been set

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.234
in three of Trump's
criminal cases

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:40.334
for stealing
classified documents,

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:41.467
trying to overturn the election,

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:42.734
and paying hush money
to a porn star.

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:44.367
Trump was caught on tape
admitting

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:45.601
that he had
secret military documents

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:46.834
that were not declassified,

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.734
kept boxes of classified
documents in his bathroom.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.234
He was found liable
for sexual abuse

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:51.634
in a civil trial,
called the former chairman

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.367
of the Joint Chiefs of Staff
to be executed,

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:54.934
reneged on a promise
to pay his ex-lawyer,

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.367
Rudy Giuliani,
who was also indicted

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.501
by a grand jury in Atlanta
for election interference

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:00.934
and is being sued by his
ex-lawyer for failure to pay,

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:03.300
as well as by Hunter Biden
for tampering with his laptop.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.400
Trump was overheard saying
the words "hang" on January 6th

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.501
as a riotous mob tried
to hang his vice president.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:08.901
Rudy was drunk
during the insurrection.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:09.968
Trump Chief of Staff
Mark Meadows

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:11.834
burned so many documents
in his fireplace

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.434
that his suit smelled
like a Boy Scout jamboree.

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.801
Ted Cruz said Barbie
is indoctrinating children

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.367
with Chinese propaganda.
The Atlantic grand jury

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:18.734
recommended an indictment
of Lindsey Graham,

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.100
among many
other Trump allies.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.767
Trump's former doctor
turned Congressman Ronny Jackson

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:24.434
got detained at a rodeo.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.033
Trump said windmills
are killing whales

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.133
and that dampening forest fires
with water would stop fires.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.501
Chris Christie called him
Donald Duck.

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.100
Marjorie Taylor Greene
showed off a giant poster board

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.634
with Hunter Biden
nudes in Congress

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.067
and confused Yom Kippur
with Hanukkah.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.133
Congressman George Santos

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.901
and Senator Bob Menendez
both indicted.

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:38.167
Mike Lindell
got mad in a lawsuit

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.601
because someone called
his pillows lumpy,

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:42.033
and Lauren Boebert got to second
base at a "Beetlejuice" musical.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.033
Did...

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:45.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:48.901
Did I miss anything?

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.767
Oh, right.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.701
Trump went to a gun store

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:57.334
and held a Glock like he was
a "Price Is Right" model.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.434
For more on much of that
as we can get to,

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:05.367
it's time for
"A Closer Look to the Max!"

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.167
-To the max.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:14.501
♪♪

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.734
-Donald Trump arrived
in New York last night

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.501
to stay at his possibly
soon-to-be-renamed residence,

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.968
Trump Tower,
ahead of his appearance today

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:30.067
at a Manhattan courthouse
for fraud trial.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.834
And I just want to say
it's really nice of him

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.634
to come back to New York
for our first show.

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:36.734
He heard the strike
was over and said,

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:40.000
[Imitating Trump]
"I can't miss 'A Closer Look.'"

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.100
[ Normal voice ]
In fact, this is very exciting.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.834
He's in the audience
with us right now.

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.367
So, if you're in the studio

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:46.300
and you hear a beeping sound,
don't worry.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:50.200
That's just his court-ordered
ankle bracelet going off.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.534
I'm just kidding.
Trump's not here.

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:53.868
He's home recuperating
after a long day of scowling.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.234
Here he is arriving
at the courthouse

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:57.467
for the fraud trial today

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:58.901
and standing there
waiting to go in

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:02.367
like a guy waiting to use
the bathroom at a concert.

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.801
[Imitating Trump]
"Come on, hurry up.

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:06.067
I want to get back to my seats
before he plays 'Piano Man.'

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.534
Where is he now?
Davy Crockett, Peter Pan,

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:12.133
Elvis Presley, Disneyland.
Alright, I got time."

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:14.667
[ Normal voice ] And then,
of course, he could not

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.968
restrain himself from launching
into an unhinged tirade

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.133
for the assembled press
where he, among other things,

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:20.868
attacked the attorney general
who brought the case

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:22.100
and the judge overseeing it.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.434
I don't want to amplify
most of what he said,

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:27.300
but here's a quick time-lapse,
just to give you an idea

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.234
of what fraud defendant
Donald Trump was doing

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:32.033
as he waited
to enter the courtroom.

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:33.601
-This is a continuation

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:37.767
of the single greatest
witch hunt of all time.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.734
She said, "Well, now I'll go
back to get Trump again,"

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:43.567
and this is what we have.
It's a scam. It's a sham.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.667
People are being murdered all
over the sidewalks of New York.

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.868
If I didn't run, I'd be sitting
right now at a beach

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.167
like Biden does every time,

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.067
even though he's supposed
to be working.

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:54.534
They have one property
that's worth

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.801
anywhere from 50 to 100 times

00:03:57.801 --> 00:04:00.701
what this judge put down
as their value -- Coca-Cola.

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:02.334
Take a look at their value.

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:03.968
They have a value.

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:05.133
The value of their brand

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.067
is more than everything else
put together.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:08.634
One other thing.

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:11.501
We have a clause in the contract

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:14.834
which tells, essentially,
"Buyer beware."

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:19.100
When you take a look
at the financial statement,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.667
don't believe anything you read.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:22.267
Do not believe anything.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:23.834
If I weren't running,

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:25.534
I wouldn't have
any of these cases.

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:28.234
I wouldn't be seeing you
this morning,

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.234
but I'll be seeing
a lot of you.

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:32.567
-"I'll be seeing a lot of you"?

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:36.300
He sounds like a creepy husband
from a Lifetime movie.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.901
[Imitating Trump] "I'll be
seeing a lot of you, Deborah.

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:41.667
You'll never find
all the cameras I installed."

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:42.767
[ Normal voice ]
By the way, that was time-lapse.

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.200
That was three days.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.834
He started Friday during the
rainstorm and hasn't stopped.

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.133
At one point, the water
was up to his waist,

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:51.400
and he still kept going.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.834
Also, generally speaking,

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.501
I would say it's not exactly
a genius legal strategy

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:58.334
to attack the judge right before
you walk into his courtroom.

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.901
"This guy's an ass [bleep]
a loser.

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:03.734
I hate his guts, and I hope
he rules in my favor."

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:05.734
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:08.400
Most of that rant was
the standard Trump word vomit,

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.234
but I do want to touch on a few
quick things like this.

00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:14.000
-The reason I got indicted
was that I ran.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.133
If I didn't run, I'd be sitting
right now at a beach

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:17.434
like Biden does every time,

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:19.734
even though he's supposed
to be working.

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:22.200
-Yeah, I just can't imagine
Donald Trump sitting on a beach.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.701
A beach implies relaxation.

00:05:23.701 --> 00:05:25.400
If Trump ever did go to a beach,

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.734
he'd spend the entire time
arguing with the seagulls.

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:29.734
[Imitating Trump]
"Excuse me, Mr. Seagull.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.167
Mr. Sea-- Those are my chips.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.000
Excuse me. I'm talking.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.000
Squawk, squawk, squawk,
squawk to you.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.834
Excuse me."

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:38.567
[ Normal voice ] But arguably,
the most bizarre thing

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:39.868
he said during his rant

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:41.734
was when he claimed
he couldn't be held liable

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:44.133
for any of the false statements
about his business assets

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:47.667
because his financial documents
have a disclaimer in them

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.667
that says nothing
in them is true.

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:52.467
-We have a clause
in the contract

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:55.868
which tells, essentially,
"Buyer beware."

00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:58.200
We have a clause
in the contract.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.968
It's like
a "buyer beware" clause.

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:04.734
It says when you take a look
at the financial statement,

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:06.367
don't believe anything you read.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:08.000
This is up front.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.634
Don't believe anything you read.

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:11.234
Some people call it
a worthless clause

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:13.901
because it makes the statement

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:15.868
and anything you read
in the statement worthless.

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:18.601
It says go out
and do your own research.

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:21.133
Go out and do your own
due diligence.

00:06:21.133 --> 00:06:23.501
You have to study
the statement carefully.

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.067
Do not believe anything.

00:06:25.067 --> 00:06:26.067
-Wait, what?

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:28.701
You can't be held liable

00:06:28.701 --> 00:06:31.467
because your business records
have a disclaimer that says,

00:06:31.467 --> 00:06:33.934
"Don't believe any of this"?

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:35.467
He's talking about
his bank records

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:38.601
like it's the warning
before an episode of "Jackass."

00:06:38.601 --> 00:06:39.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:43.234
Do his tax returns also say,
"Don't try this at home"?

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.968
So, then after he spent
a few minutes

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:48.167
further incriminating himself,
Trump entered the courtroom

00:06:48.167 --> 00:06:50.100
where he sat down
at the defense table.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:53.868
And as you can see from these
images, he's having a blast.

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:56.033
Generally speaking,
if you're an alleged criminal

00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:58.033
trying to look innocent
at a fraud trial,

00:06:58.033 --> 00:07:01.000
I would not go
with menacing scowl.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.267
If you didn't know the context
and just saw his face,

00:07:03.267 --> 00:07:07.067
you'd think he was on trial
for all the murders.

00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:09.901
That's his audition tape
to play a Klingon general.

00:07:09.901 --> 00:07:11.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.234 --> 00:07:12.434
But I have to say,

00:07:12.434 --> 00:07:14.133
the scene that I found
especially incredible

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:16.601
was this shot of
Attorney General Letitia James

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:19.067
perfectly positioned
in the background,

00:07:19.067 --> 00:07:20.567
over Trump's shoulder,
staring at --

00:07:20.567 --> 00:07:22.667
look at that shot!

00:07:22.667 --> 00:07:24.000
What cinematography!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.767
Did they get the same director
who did "Succession"?

00:07:26.767 --> 00:07:28.133
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.133 --> 00:07:30.434
The only thing --
[ Applause ]

00:07:30.434 --> 00:07:32.033
Wonderful.

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:34.901
The only thing missing
from this scene was Cousin Greg.

00:07:34.901 --> 00:07:37.234
What's Trump saying
in the courtroom, Greg?

00:07:37.234 --> 00:07:40.601
"Uh, I think he's, uh,
suggesting that, uh, perhaps

00:07:40.601 --> 00:07:43.067
in terms of the, uh,
jurisprudence

00:07:43.067 --> 00:07:45.934
of -- of the, uh, uh, legal
proceedings,

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:48.934
that he's, um, uh, completely
[bleep]"

00:07:48.934 --> 00:07:52.501
Now, in a way,
Trump has already lost this case

00:07:52.501 --> 00:07:54.067
before he stepped foot
in the courtroom

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:55.701
because last week,
before the trial even began,

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:57.000
the judge found Trump
had lied about

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.334
his business assets for years.

00:07:58.334 --> 00:08:00.868
And now, the attorney general
is asking the judge

00:08:00.868 --> 00:08:03.300
to bar him from doing business
in New York,

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.300
which means Trump
could lose everything.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:08.801
-We begin with a major ruling
in a civil case

00:08:08.801 --> 00:08:12.334
against Donald Trump
and his family business.

00:08:12.334 --> 00:08:17.501
In a 35-page decision yesterday,
Manhattan judge Arthur Engoron

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:21.534
found the former president
and his two oldest sons

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:25.267
and their companies
liable for fraud.

00:08:25.267 --> 00:08:26.734
The judge found Trump

00:08:26.734 --> 00:08:30.000
"repeatedly submitted
fraudulent financial documents

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.467
about the value
of his assets to banks

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:33.934
and other insurance companies,"

00:08:33.934 --> 00:08:36.734
and that his financial
statements were

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:40.467
"based in a fantasy world,
not the real world."

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:42.634
The attorney general's team
sought to convince the judge

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:45.801
in this case that Trump should
be barred from doing business

00:08:45.801 --> 00:08:47.133
in the state of New York.

00:08:47.133 --> 00:08:49.300
-The former president
could eventually lose control

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:51.501
of iconic properties
like Trump Tower.

00:08:51.501 --> 00:08:53.634
-Is it clear?
Does he have $250 million?

00:08:53.634 --> 00:08:58.901
If that was an actual penalty
that the company was to pay?

00:08:58.901 --> 00:09:00.534
-I'm not sure how liquid
he is at the moment

00:09:00.534 --> 00:09:01.834
and whether he could pay that,

00:09:01.834 --> 00:09:03.334
but this is obviously
a big question

00:09:03.334 --> 00:09:05.167
is what his actual assets are.

00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:06.767
-That's right -- Trump might
not even have the money

00:09:06.767 --> 00:09:08.634
to pay the penalty
in his fraud trial,

00:09:08.634 --> 00:09:11.033
which means there's a remote
but realistic possibility

00:09:11.033 --> 00:09:12.634
that Trump Tower
gets taken away,

00:09:12.634 --> 00:09:14.033
he has to sell Mar-a-Lago,

00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:16.934
and he ends up crashing
with Rudy Giuliani.

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:18.367
[Imitating Trump]
"I call top bunk."

00:09:18.367 --> 00:09:20.067
[Imitating Giuliani] "But,
Boss, I don't have a bunk bed."

00:09:20.067 --> 00:09:21.567
[Imitating Trump] "You can sleep
under the mattress."

00:09:21.567 --> 00:09:23.834
[Imitating Giuliani]
"Oh, this is great.

00:09:23.834 --> 00:09:25.968
Maybe this will finally
straighten out my neck.

00:09:25.968 --> 00:09:27.767
My chiropractor says
I have a condition

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:29.667
called Gargoyle Spine."

00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:31.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:31.667 --> 00:09:33.901
So, the actual trial
began today.

00:09:33.901 --> 00:09:36.434
Trump and his lopsided adult
sons are on the witness list,

00:09:36.434 --> 00:09:40.033
but the judge in the case
has already effectively ruled

00:09:40.033 --> 00:09:41.501
that the facts
are not in dispute.

00:09:41.501 --> 00:09:42.834
He wrote in his ruling

00:09:42.834 --> 00:09:45.567
that Trump's inflated claims
about his business assets

00:09:45.567 --> 00:09:47.434
constitute obvious fraud.

00:09:47.434 --> 00:09:51.267
-The judge effectively decided
he didn't need a trial

00:09:51.267 --> 00:09:54.133
to determine
the Trumps were liable.

00:09:54.133 --> 00:09:55.701
The judge wrote
in his ruling,

00:09:55.701 --> 00:09:58.234
"This is a fantasy world,
not the real world,"

00:09:58.234 --> 00:10:00.501
and admonished
the former president

00:10:00.501 --> 00:10:07.734
for his overvaluing his holdings
by as much as $2.2 billion.

00:10:07.734 --> 00:10:10.033
In one example,
Trump overestimated

00:10:10.033 --> 00:10:13.033
the size
of his Manhattan apartment,

00:10:13.033 --> 00:10:15.100
which he spent years living in,

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:20.801
by 19,000 feet, or 200%.

00:10:20.801 --> 00:10:23.634
Judge Engoron called that
absurd, writing,

00:10:23.634 --> 00:10:26.167
"a discrepancy of this order
of magnitude

00:10:26.167 --> 00:10:28.367
by a real estate developer

00:10:28.367 --> 00:10:31.734
sizing up his own living space
of decades

00:10:31.734 --> 00:10:33.934
can only be considered fraud."

00:10:33.934 --> 00:10:37.000
-Trump inflated
his own apartment size by 200%.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.367
In other words,
he tripled it.

00:10:38.367 --> 00:10:40.634
I wouldn't be surprised
if the photos were fake, too.

00:10:40.634 --> 00:10:42.934
Remember how we all thought
it looked like this?

00:10:42.934 --> 00:10:44.200
That's photoshopped.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.634
If you remove the filter,
it looks like this.

00:10:46.634 --> 00:10:48.501
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.501 --> 00:10:51.267
This ruling undercuts
his entire mythology.

00:10:51.267 --> 00:10:52.601
Everything about him is a lie.

00:10:52.601 --> 00:10:54.701
Not only were his businesses
and net worth inflated,

00:10:54.701 --> 00:10:56.701
but he even pretended
his own apartment

00:10:56.701 --> 00:10:58.234
was three times bigger
than it actually was.

00:10:58.234 --> 00:11:00.601
Next, we're going to find out
he and Melania are just friends.

00:11:00.601 --> 00:11:01.868
I'm kidding.
Friends like each other.

00:11:01.868 --> 00:11:06.367
And yet, somehow, this fraud
trial could very well --

00:11:06.367 --> 00:11:08.234
very well be the least
of Trump's concerns.

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:09.534
As we all know,

00:11:09.534 --> 00:11:12.234
he's got four upcoming
criminal cases to deal with,

00:11:12.234 --> 00:11:15.033
and trial dates have been set
for three of those cases.

00:11:15.033 --> 00:11:17.934
We'll tell you all about that,
right after this break.

00:11:17.934 --> 00:11:19.701
Wait. We're allowed
to do a commercial

00:11:19.701 --> 00:11:21.534
during "A Closer Look?"
Is that a new thing?

00:11:21.534 --> 00:11:23.100
Alright.
Let's see how it goes.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:25.033 --> 00:11:26.968
Now, as I was saying...

00:11:28.701 --> 00:11:31.834
...before I was
so rudely interrupted

00:11:31.834 --> 00:11:33.801
by our incredibly
valuable advertisers --

00:11:33.801 --> 00:11:35.267
thank you so much.

00:11:36.267 --> 00:11:37.767
On top of the civil fraud trial

00:11:37.767 --> 00:11:39.467
Trump appeared at today
in Manhattan,

00:11:39.467 --> 00:11:41.901
he's also, of course,
facing four indictments --

00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:44.234
three more, it should be noted,
than the Unabomber,

00:11:44.234 --> 00:11:47.634
who, as the "Una" implies,
had just the one.

00:11:47.634 --> 00:11:49.100
One of Trump's indictments,
of course, involves

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.234
the classified documents
he stole from the White House,

00:11:51.234 --> 00:11:53.734
and at the House GOP
sham impeachment hearing

00:11:53.734 --> 00:11:55.200
into Joe Biden last week,

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:58.601
Congresswoman Jasmine Crockett
compared the stolen documents,

00:11:58.601 --> 00:12:00.467
some of which were found
in Trump's bathroom,

00:12:00.467 --> 00:12:01.901
to the allegations
against Biden

00:12:01.901 --> 00:12:04.968
with an especially memorable
choice of words.

00:12:04.968 --> 00:12:08.467
-As I walked
into this chamber today,

00:12:08.467 --> 00:12:11.534
as I prepared, I said,
"What is the crime?"

00:12:11.534 --> 00:12:13.567
Because when you're talking
about impeachment,

00:12:13.567 --> 00:12:17.501
you're talking about
high crimes or misdemeanors.

00:12:17.501 --> 00:12:20.200
And I can't seem
to find the crime.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:23.367
And honestly, no one
has testified of what crime

00:12:23.367 --> 00:12:26.834
they believe the President of
the United States has committed.

00:12:26.834 --> 00:12:30.000
But when we start talking about
things that look like evidence,

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.334
they want to act
like they blind.

00:12:31.334 --> 00:12:32.400
They don't know what this is.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:35.067
These are our national secrets,

00:12:35.067 --> 00:12:37.267
looks like in the [bleep] to me.

00:12:37.267 --> 00:12:39.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:39.667 --> 00:12:40.934
-Yep.

00:12:40.934 --> 00:12:43.167
Much like the country
when he was in office,

00:12:43.167 --> 00:12:45.534
Trump left his classified
documents in the [bleep]

00:12:45.534 --> 00:12:47.901
And I really appreciate
that choice of words

00:12:47.901 --> 00:12:50.567
because it accurately captures
the decor of Trump's bathroom.

00:12:50.567 --> 00:12:52.667
It doesn't look like
a powder room or a lavatory.

00:12:52.667 --> 00:12:54.300
It looks like a [bleep]
fancy [bleep]

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:56.601
but it's a [bleep] nonetheless.

00:12:56.601 --> 00:12:58.968
I mean, put aside the fact
that there are boxes

00:12:58.968 --> 00:13:01.334
of stolen classified documents
in there, you know,

00:13:01.334 --> 00:13:03.334
just in case you run out of
Golf Digests

00:13:03.334 --> 00:13:04.534
or "Family Circuses."

00:13:04.534 --> 00:13:07.701
He's got a fancy chandelier

00:13:07.701 --> 00:13:09.400
right next
to a cheap curtain rod.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:12.033
I don't think I've ever seen
a weirder combination

00:13:12.033 --> 00:13:14.334
of expensive and chintzy choices
in a bathroom before.

00:13:14.334 --> 00:13:17.200
It's like a porta-potty
with monogrammed towels.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.467
[ Laughter ]

00:13:18.467 --> 00:13:20.200
If you're going to lay out
for the chandelier,

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.400
why not just get
a proper shower installed

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.901
or a sliding glass door
or something?

00:13:23.901 --> 00:13:26.801
This looks like the bathroom
at a funeral home in Yonkers.

00:13:26.801 --> 00:13:28.067
And by the way,

00:13:28.067 --> 00:13:31.167
you know Trump calls it
the [bleep] too.

00:13:31.167 --> 00:13:33.634
Like, when he's on his private
jet with his gang of weirdos

00:13:33.634 --> 00:13:35.367
complaining about the bathroom
being occupied.

00:13:35.367 --> 00:13:36.567
[Imitating Trump]
"Where's Rudy?"

00:13:36.567 --> 00:13:38.000
[ Normal voice ]
"He's still in the [bleep] sir.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.267
Sometimes he breathes
in too much hair dye

00:13:40.267 --> 00:13:41.567
and passes out in there."

00:13:41.567 --> 00:13:43.033
[Imitating Giuliani]
"Boss! It happened again.

00:13:43.033 --> 00:13:45.501
I had the craziest dream where
I was the president's lawyer.

00:13:45.501 --> 00:13:46.801
I am?!"

00:13:46.801 --> 00:13:48.567
[ Laughter ]

00:13:48.567 --> 00:13:49.801
[ Normal voice ]
And while we're on the subject,

00:13:49.801 --> 00:13:51.334
you might be wondering
how Republicans

00:13:51.334 --> 00:13:52.701
could have possibly
defended this.

00:13:52.701 --> 00:13:55.901
Here's soon-to-be-former
House Speaker Kevin McCarthy

00:13:55.901 --> 00:13:59.334
offering a defense of Trump's
bathroom/filing cabinet

00:13:59.334 --> 00:14:00.501
back in June.

00:14:10.701 --> 00:14:13.133
Yeah, bathroom...
[ Laughter ]

00:14:13.133 --> 00:14:15.267
Bathroom doors lock
so you can pee in private,

00:14:15.267 --> 00:14:19.133
not so you can use it
as a home safe.

00:14:19.133 --> 00:14:20.601
Also, the bathroom door
kind of famously

00:14:20.601 --> 00:14:22.000
has the flimsiest lock
in the house.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.300
If you're watching
a horror movie

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:25.200
and a character runs into
the bathroom and locks the door,

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:26.334
say your goodbyes.

00:14:26.334 --> 00:14:29.000
There isn't a single normal
human being

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.634
who keeps important
things in the bathroom.

00:14:30.634 --> 00:14:32.601
"Hey, honey, where's
our marriage certificate?"

00:14:32.601 --> 00:14:35.434
"It's next to the plunger."

00:14:35.434 --> 00:14:38.267
Also, a bathroom door
only locks from the inside.

00:14:38.267 --> 00:14:40.267
If no one's in there,
it's open.

00:14:40.267 --> 00:14:43.801
So, what you're saying is
our nation's most sensitive

00:14:43.801 --> 00:14:45.367
and highly guarded secrets
are safe,

00:14:45.367 --> 00:14:47.534
as long as someone's
in there taking a dump.

00:14:47.534 --> 00:14:51.734
Do we assign someone from the
archives department to that job,

00:14:51.734 --> 00:14:54.534
or is that more
of a Secret Service thing?

00:14:54.534 --> 00:14:57.300
"Agent Callahan, your bathroom
shift starts at 5:00 a.m.

00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:00.467
Better start pounding
some bran."

00:15:00.467 --> 00:15:02.334
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:15:02.334 --> 00:15:05.200
So, the faraway frontrunner
for the GOP nomination

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:08.467
is facing four indictments
and a civil fraud case

00:15:08.467 --> 00:15:09.834
that could end
his entire business.

00:15:09.834 --> 00:15:11.133
But fair is fair.

00:15:11.133 --> 00:15:12.501
And I do want to give
the Republican Party credit.

00:15:12.501 --> 00:15:14.467
I'm happy to report that
in the five months

00:15:14.467 --> 00:15:17.133
since we were last on the air,
the GOP has undergone

00:15:17.133 --> 00:15:19.000
a radical transformation
into a serious,

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.467
sober-minded collection
of diligent professionals

00:15:21.467 --> 00:15:23.701
capable of
competently administering

00:15:23.701 --> 00:15:24.767
the basic functions
of government.

00:15:24.767 --> 00:15:25.834
And I'm just kidding.

00:15:25.834 --> 00:15:27.434
It's still a giant
ass-over-teakettle

00:15:27.434 --> 00:15:28.434
cluster [bleep]

00:15:28.434 --> 00:15:31.801
-This is CNN Breaking News.

00:15:31.801 --> 00:15:33.067
-Good evening, everyone.

00:15:33.067 --> 00:15:36.234
This is CNN special live
coverage on a chaotic night,

00:15:36.234 --> 00:15:38.400
even by Washington standards.

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.834
I'm Dana Bash,
live in the nation's capital.

00:15:40.834 --> 00:15:42.100
Here's the headline.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.634
The United States government
will not shut down,

00:15:44.634 --> 00:15:47.100
at least not
for another 45 days.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:50.634
-The House Speaker had his back
up against the wall, it seems.

00:15:50.634 --> 00:15:51.868
He was not going to get anywhere

00:15:51.868 --> 00:15:54.501
with his Republican
conference alone.

00:15:54.501 --> 00:15:55.667
There was just
too much infighting

00:15:55.667 --> 00:15:57.667
going on inside the conference.

00:15:57.667 --> 00:16:00.801
And so, he had to work with
Democrats to get this done here.

00:16:00.801 --> 00:16:03.801
-This all comes, Jake,
as the tension was palpable

00:16:03.801 --> 00:16:05.400
among some of the Republicans.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.801
-The fate of House Speaker
Kevin McCarthy

00:16:07.801 --> 00:16:11.400
is uncertain at this time
as hardliners in his party

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.167
are pushing for his ouster.

00:16:13.167 --> 00:16:16.400
-Do you still support him,
Mr. Speaker?

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:18.167
-I had my questions.
I have my doubts.

00:16:18.167 --> 00:16:22.400
-We cannot blame the Democrats
for having not done our job.

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:23.801
-This is a huge mess.

00:16:23.801 --> 00:16:26.000
-I've been frustrated
by the process.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.868
I thought we would be
better than this.

00:16:27.868 --> 00:16:29.067
-"Yeah, we're Republicans.

00:16:29.067 --> 00:16:30.567
We're supposed to be
better than this.

00:16:30.567 --> 00:16:32.601
We're the party of serious
statesmen like Rudy Giuliani,

00:16:32.601 --> 00:16:34.067
Marjorie Taylor Greene,
Mike Lindell,

00:16:34.067 --> 00:16:36.267
and the lady who got horned up
at the 'Beetlejuice' musical."

00:16:36.267 --> 00:16:38.067
Seriously, Republicans,

00:16:38.067 --> 00:16:40.467
why did you think
you would be better than this?

00:16:40.467 --> 00:16:42.434
Did you forget
the entire Trump presidency?

00:16:42.434 --> 00:16:44.300
And if so, can you send me
some of the pills

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:46.000
that helped you do that?

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.901
You're like a Jets fan saying,
"I think this is our year,"

00:16:48.901 --> 00:16:51.067
after Aaron Rodgers went down.

00:16:51.067 --> 00:16:52.367
[ Applause ]

00:16:52.367 --> 00:16:53.901
So, Republicans
basically caused

00:16:53.901 --> 00:16:55.968
a bunch of pointless chaos
and paralysis,

00:16:55.968 --> 00:16:57.567
pushing us to the brink
of a shutdown

00:16:57.567 --> 00:17:00.133
that would imperil millions of
Americans' paychecks and jobs.

00:17:00.133 --> 00:17:02.534
And in the end, they had to be
bailed out by Democrats,

00:17:02.534 --> 00:17:04.601
who supplied most of the votes
to keep the government open.

00:17:04.601 --> 00:17:07.400
And now, because of that,
GOP hardliner Matt Gaetz,

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:10.067
McCarthy's chief antagonist
in the GOP caucus,

00:17:10.067 --> 00:17:12.334
is threatening to stir up
even more chaos

00:17:12.334 --> 00:17:15.200
by filing a motion
to remove McCarthy as Speaker.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:18.133
-The future of Kevin McCarthy's
speakership is in peril

00:17:18.133 --> 00:17:19.634
after he teamed up
with Democrats

00:17:19.634 --> 00:17:21.100
to avert a government shutdown.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:22.701
Well, this morning,
Congressman Matt Gaetz

00:17:22.701 --> 00:17:26.133
says that he is moving forward
with a motion to vacate

00:17:26.133 --> 00:17:29.133
to try to oust
McCarthy as Speaker.

00:17:29.133 --> 00:17:31.033
-I do intend to file
a motion to vacate

00:17:31.033 --> 00:17:33.000
against Speaker McCarthy
this week.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.067
-He says he's coming for you.
Can you survive?

00:17:35.067 --> 00:17:36.701
-Yes, I'll survive.

00:17:36.701 --> 00:17:39.968
-Oof, that's the worst Gloria
Gaynor cover I've ever heard.

00:17:39.968 --> 00:17:43.400
Gaetz vs. McCarthy is a real
"Alien vs. Predator" situation.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:46.234
In fact, Gaetz and the alien
have the same size forehead,

00:17:46.234 --> 00:17:47.667
so that's pretty cool.

00:17:47.667 --> 00:17:49.334
So, the result,
keeping the government open,

00:17:49.334 --> 00:17:50.868
must have been a relief
for millions of Americans,

00:17:50.868 --> 00:17:52.133
including Joe Biden.

00:17:52.133 --> 00:17:54.734
Although I will say
if the government had shut down,

00:17:54.734 --> 00:17:57.133
I was kind of hoping Biden would
follow the late night host lead

00:17:57.133 --> 00:17:59.067
and start a podcast
with the other living presidents

00:17:59.067 --> 00:18:00.567
called "Air Force Five."

00:18:00.567 --> 00:18:02.567
[ Laughter ]

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.367
[Imitating Biden] "Today's
episode is brought to you

00:18:06.367 --> 00:18:10.133
by Manscape, the world leader
in male grooming."

00:18:10.133 --> 00:18:12.334
[Imitating Obama]
"Oh, Manscape delivers

00:18:12.334 --> 00:18:18.834
a peak performance...
for your most sensitive areas."

00:18:18.834 --> 00:18:21.801
[Imitating Clinton]
"I feel your pain

00:18:21.801 --> 00:18:26.033
when you use inferior grooming
tools."

00:18:26.033 --> 00:18:27.667
[Imitating Carter]
"America..."

00:18:27.667 --> 00:18:30.667
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:18:32.601 --> 00:18:35.000
"America, I'm 99 years old,

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:38.734
and I still use
this product every day."

00:18:38.734 --> 00:18:42.000
[Imitating Bush]
"Go to Manscape.com today.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.000
Use promo code Bush."

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.000
[ Laughter ]

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:18:48.234 --> 00:18:50.400
"For 20% off...

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.400
your man bush."

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.467
[ Normal voice ]
Thank you.

00:18:53.467 --> 00:18:54.934
Five...

00:18:56.167 --> 00:18:58.734
Five months
in impression camp paid off.

00:18:58.734 --> 00:19:01.334
We did one president
a month, obviously.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:06.868
I've got a little rushed
on Carter month.

00:19:08.934 --> 00:19:10.667
Republicans spent weeks
devouring each other

00:19:10.667 --> 00:19:12.200
and self-immolating
to the point

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:14.033
that they couldn't be bothered
to keep the government open

00:19:14.033 --> 00:19:15.234
until Democrats bailed them out.

00:19:15.234 --> 00:19:16.467
And that's because
they were focused

00:19:16.467 --> 00:19:18.868
on an even more
embarrassing spectacle --

00:19:18.868 --> 00:19:20.834
an impeachment hearing
into Joe Biden,

00:19:20.834 --> 00:19:23.167
where even Republicans admitted
they humiliated themselves.

00:19:23.167 --> 00:19:26.133
We'll show you some of
the lowlights right after this.

00:19:26.133 --> 00:19:27.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:19:27.868 --> 00:19:30.133
As we told you before the break,
Republicans

00:19:30.133 --> 00:19:32.234
could barely be bothered
to keep the government open

00:19:32.234 --> 00:19:34.234
and had to turn to the Democrats
to bail them out.

00:19:34.234 --> 00:19:35.567
Now, you might be
asking yourself

00:19:35.567 --> 00:19:37.968
what could have
possibly been more important

00:19:37.968 --> 00:19:39.367
than keeping
the government functioning?

00:19:39.367 --> 00:19:42.167
What else was
the GOP focused on?

00:19:42.167 --> 00:19:44.767
-The House GOP is focused
on Hunter Biden,

00:19:44.767 --> 00:19:47.567
spending this entire Thursday
morning and afternoon,

00:19:47.567 --> 00:19:50.033
again, just two days
before the government shuts down

00:19:50.033 --> 00:19:52.934
on Saturday, to open
their impeachment inquiry

00:19:52.934 --> 00:19:55.100
into his dad, the president.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:56.734
They're looking into
Hunter Biden, as well.

00:19:56.734 --> 00:19:59.534
-Even some Republicans this
morning are privately grumbling

00:19:59.534 --> 00:20:02.334
about how that first
impeachment hearing went.

00:20:02.334 --> 00:20:04.634
No bombshells,
no direct evidence

00:20:04.634 --> 00:20:07.067
that President Biden
did anything wrong.

00:20:07.067 --> 00:20:09.033
-I want to emphasize

00:20:09.033 --> 00:20:12.801
what it is that
we're here today for.

00:20:12.801 --> 00:20:16.167
This is a question
of an impeachment inquiry.

00:20:16.167 --> 00:20:19.400
It is not a vote
on articles of impeachment.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:23.067
In fact, I do not believe
that the current evidence

00:20:23.067 --> 00:20:25.767
would support articles
of impeachment.

00:20:25.767 --> 00:20:28.267
-That's your first witness?!

00:20:28.267 --> 00:20:30.400
He just came out and [bleep]
all over your whole case.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:32.367
That's like if the best man
at your wedding

00:20:32.367 --> 00:20:33.567
got up to give a toast
and said,

